        {
          "propertyId": "a126ca530c8e48d5b88882c734c38935",
          "spaceId": "dac259bad48a11adf97fe36857d85206",
          "text": "Equal study weights do not resolve bias in class-size research.",
          "decimal": null,
          "integer": null,
          "boolean": null
        },
        {
          "propertyId": "84dacbddca6a44079edb5e11a4c66b40",
          "spaceId": "dac259bad48a11adf97fe36857d85206",
          "text": "Chapter 2, The importance of quality, printed pp. 46–50; conclusion p. 61",
          "decimal": null,
          "integer": null,
          "boolean": null
        },
        {
          "propertyId": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037",
          "spaceId": "dac259bad48a11adf97fe36857d85206",
          "text": "Hanushek (2002) argues that Krueger’s reweighting favors weaker estimates. He emphasizes omitted state policies and prior educational inputs when judging study quality.",
          "decimal": null,
          "integer": null,
          "boolean": null
        }
      ]
    },
